people here say that they could see  bodies literally dropping from the skies  huge passenger jet coming down in the  middle of a war zone that's gonna be a  big story it didn't seem like a real  situation it's being a tall I've just  never seen so many dead people  [Music]  it was unbelievable I've been in Israel  would you believe and and I was waiting  to go into Gaza we were doing a live  shot when suddenly this news broke  break-in used to bring you the Reuters  news agency reporting that a Malaysian a  passenger aeroplane has crashed in  Ukraine Oh Cameron said to me this NH 17  is crash it's very unlucky and I said  that's not unlucky that's been shot down  it was rumoured that the plane had been  shot down by a surface-to-air missile  that kind of thing doesn't happen every  day well try and find out more details  from the scene I was working in the sky  newsroom that day I think initially we  all thought well this must be a mistake  it can't be a passenger jet it's it's a  military aircraft for so many weeks we'd  had reports of Ukrainian aircraft being  shot at by pro-russian separatists in  that exact region but as the reports  continued to come in we realized that  actually it was much bigger than that  so the newsroom becomes this kind of  frenetic place people are running around  trying to make sure that we're getting  this story on air correctly reporting  the facts hundreds of passengers are  feared dead after a Malaysian Airlines  jet crashed in Ukraine there are claims  the plane may have been shot down with  both Ukrainian government and  pro-russian separatists denying  responsibility our foreign desk really  springs into action the key job that  they have to do is make sure we've got  people on the ground we've got the call  to go to Ukraine  weirdly Ukraine on Israel have so many  flights you couldn't you couldn't you  know you couldn't imagine how many  flights there are nobody else to get to  Ukraine but we did we jumped on the  plane that evening seven hours later  we're at the crash site  they were going to have to send a big  deployment multiple teams multiple  people to go and report this story I  kind of stuck my hand up and said look I  can go right away you can see was gonna  be a massive story a huge passenger jet  at Boeing triple7 coming down in the  middle of a war zone that's gonna be a  big story we navigated our own way and  eventually saw some debris in the field  I came over the hill of a corn field and  at the bottom I could see wreckage  burning I said to Pete this is still on  fire we saw it's unbelievable  we didn't expect to get anywhere near  the epicenter of the crash site we were  I think just mesmerised that we actually  got there and then with what we were  faced with we were so fresh on the  ground less than 24 hours after the  plane had come down all the bodies were  we're still lying there compared to  other stories I've done of natural  disasters and war zones this this was  high up there  everywhere I look the bodies I mean just  heads and arms and legs and young  children and suitcases and and just  people everywhere every step in trees  tops of houses is staggering and I think  that's absolutely staggering I've just  never seen so many dead people in one  place at any at just one time  to be kind of launched into the middle  of a crash site of a huge passenger  plane  it just blew both of our minds we saw  such a catastrophic incident that as the  plane broke up people here say that they  could see bodies literally dropping from  the skies  [Music]  I was filming Stuart in the what was the  wings section and that where the engines  are  he could smell bodies you could smell  death  [Music]  you saw parts of aircraft stood around  the countryside and then obviously  people's personal effects  and then you pull up actually to the  main crash site itself which is enormous  they're still pulling bodies out of the  crash line  [Music]  none of it seemed real it didn't seem  like a real situation to being at all  there we were stood right on the middle  of the main croissant there were  probably 20-30 body stretching ahead of  us  [Music]  horrendous  the debris field I think is the is the  term they used was very large we were at  one end at the debris field but it went  back a long long way in the whole way  through fields after fields and roads  after rosin body just ever way you long  the access to the crash zone was  absolutely incredible it wouldn't happen  in the UK or anywhere else in the  Western world but there we were right on  the edge of this major crash site where  a passenger jet had fallen from the sky  there was no order whatsoever there were  military there but there was no one  actually preventing us from from doing  anything it's just totally serene  nothing was cordoned off everything  could be accessed and seen and genuinely  you were standing in amongst this  wreckage we walked through a bit of a  track out into the field itself and  suddenly opened up into an area will the  crops were flattened there ahead of us  basically was the front of the part of  the aircraft  who's there very obviously the the  cockpit and the business car section you  can see the pilot seats you can see all  the avionics you can see cables and  control panels just strewn everywhere  there was paperwork there was flight  logs and briefcases with the details of  that day's flight on it all these items  that made the thing incredibly human so  poignant and so sad in the wreckage you  saw the actual handwritten note that  their captain would have said over the  tunnel  it's not where do we was we - I had  never seen anything like it on the hands  of the wheel of the in the coping with  her hands of the the guy who had been  flying a plane and we did a piece the  camera it Pete says we can't use this  and wait since our hand it's still on  the wheel  [Music]  I've never been in a situation like this  before you know I've been in war zones  many times and I've been to smaller  plane crashes but I've never been to a  large plane crash in the middle of a war  zone behind me I can hear you won't be  able to hear it but there's a grad  missile launcher that has been firing  pretty much every 10 minutes for the  last few hours there is a battle taking  place a few kilometers away we're in the  middle of a war but it was fighting  going on all around us while we were  looking at this huge graves all you  could hear was the boom of artillery  I must confess I really wasn't thinking  about the the danger aspects of it I  wasn't thinking about that being an  active pretty hairy war zone the area of  the crash there were some flower fields  and cornfields and locals has  effectively brought a white flag on a  stick marking a body or part of a body  I remember seeing that local people have  come from nearby towns and villages  there was a group of coal miners who'd  come to help with the recovery efforts  we pulled up it's a field where we saw a  lot of activity and basically it was  people doing a long line search through  the crops and it was quite extraordinary  it was a beautiful picture if you like  because the crops are so pretty in the  sunlight but you know that they're  actually looking for bodies and every  time they found a body they'd put a  stick in the ground with a little white  piece of material on it and that would  mark the body that will stay with me  [Music]  it took a really long time for the  repatriation to get underway first they  had to account for all of the victims  and then transport them from the crash  site  to Ukrainian friendly territory and that  was where they were going to be flown on  their final journey home  [Music]  so the first time that the bodies were  actually dealt with with any sort of  dignity  they were handed over and then  everything kind of slowed down and  bodies were calmly  loaded onto the back of the transport  planes it was almost like a military  funeral very very respectful  [Music]  when a Plane full of women men children  who were probably just going on holiday  shot out of the sky by a myth harlot  that should not have happened  I think that was really difficult to  process and I really hope I don't never  have to cover a story like that again  why they would want to shoot a passenger  jet down I do not know the only thing I  can think is that it was unintentional  military jets and helicopters have been  shot down but why they would suddenly  then want to start targeting a passenger  jet I just I just don't understand  there was a major investigation and that  found that the missile system used to  shoot down the airliner had to come from  Russia but of course the Russians deny  that and the whole thing just goes on  and on it was only when you started to  think about the families and and  everything that they had gone through  it's quite stressful  [Music]  my sympathy would go to the obviously  the families who have not got closure  yet I just hope that comes soon  [Music]  [Applause]

